      "quoted_tweet_id": null,
      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "The U.S. Border Patrol mourns the loss of Border Patrol Agent Sean M. McDonough.\n \nAgent McDonough began his USBP career in 2007 and most recently served at the Wellesley Island Border Patrol Station in the Buffalo Sector, New York. Over the course of his service, he also served at the Nogales Station and in the Houlton Sector. Prior to joining USBP, he honorably served in the U.S. Army, the Army National Guard, and as a Military Police Officer.\n \nAgent McDonough dedicated his life to serving his country and protecting the American people.\n \nOur deepest condolences go out to his family, friends, and fellow agents during this difficult time.\n\n@USBPChiefBUN",
      "text_resolved": "The U.S. Border Patrol mourns the loss of Border Patrol Agent Sean M. McDonough.\n \nAgent McDonough began his USBP career in 2007 and most recently served at the Wellesley Island Border Patrol Station in the Buffalo Sector, New York. Over the course of his service, he also served at the Nogales Station and in the Houlton Sector. Prior to joining USBP, he honorably served in the U.S. Army, the Army National Guard, and as a Military Police Officer.\n \nAgent McDonough dedicated his life to serving his country and protecting the American people.\n \nOur deepest condolences go out to his family, friends, and fellow agents during this difficult time.\n\n@USBPChiefBUN",
